{
  "_schema_note": "positions.<TICKER> fields, all routine-derived cache -- never authoritative; positions.yaml (broker) is the only truth for shares/avg_cost, and any conflict is resolved in broker's favor. highest_alerted_profit_tier / highest_alerted_stop_tier / highest_alerted_add_tier: each 0-3, monotonic within its own cycle, never decreases except via a defined reset. current_stage: IDLE/TIER1/TIER2/TIER3, profit side only. rsi_peak / hourly_rsi_peak / highest_price_since_buy: max seen this profit cycle. swing_high: pullback-calc reference for add-on suggestions, separate from highest_price_since_buy, resets to the trigger price after a successful add suggestion (not after every run). dca_watch_stage/dca_watch_low/dca_watch_started_at: the IDLE->WATCHING state machine that tracks an in-progress pullback. dca_executed_count: how many add-on suggestions have actually been sent this cycle (informational -- nothing auto-executes). peak_shares_since_buy / peak_marked_swing_high: for the remaining-position DCA cap and its unlock condition. last_dca_trigger_trading_day: cooldown reference. last_action_category/last_action_date: for Action Lock (REDUCE_SELL vs ADD same-day exclusivity). last_avg_cost/last_shares: mirrors positions.yaml, refreshed every run unconditionally. Reset rules (from T-1 close vs avg_cost, not intraday price): t1_close < avg_cost resets profit-tier fields only; t1_close >= avg_cost resets highest_alerted_stop_tier only (mutually exclusive by definition). A same-cycle avg_cost/shares change (add-on or dilution, shares stays > 0 throughout) resets ONLY the add/watch fields (highest_alerted_add_tier, dca_watch_stage/low/started_at) -- never resets profit-tier or stop-tier memory, and peak_shares_since_buy bumps up to the new share count if it's higher. Full liquidation (shares 0 -> reappearing) resets everything. A ticker missing from state.json is first-run init, not a reset.",
